{
  "title": "Clean up Snapshot | Mapping union types introduced by snapshot dataclass migration",
  "description": "PR #1249 migrated SnapshotPlayer, CombatGroup, and Snapshot from TypedDict to dataclass. To avoid breaking the v7-to-v8 migration script (which passes raw dicts), compute_aftermath_index in blunder_eval_common.py was changed to accept Sequence[Snapshot | Mapping[str, object]] and uses export_record_field() instead of direct attribute access.\n\
\n\
The right fix: have the migration script coerce its snapshots before calling compute_aftermath_index, then simplify the function back to Sequence[Snapshot] with direct .seq / .ts access. This removes the polymorphic accessor and makes the function type-safe again.\n\
\n\
Locations:\n\
- scripts/analysis/blunder_eval_common.py: compute_aftermath_index signature and body\n\
- schemas/migrations/v7_to_v8.py: caller that passes raw dicts",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "typing",
    "refactor",
    "schemas",
  ],
